course: dictionary
lesson: 7013
title: Parenthesis: extra information in a sentence
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Parenthesis is extra information added into a sentence. You can mark it with brackets, a pair of dashes or a pair of commas. «My dog (a spaniel) loves walks.» The words in brackets are the extra part.
explain: Use the lift-out check: if you can take the marked part out and still have a full sentence, it is parenthesis. «Mum, who is a nurse, works nights.» Take out «who is a nurse» and you still have «Mum works nights.»
explain: Parenthesis is a noun, so one is a parenthesis and more than one are parentheses. In maths, brackets around a part of a sum tell you to work that part out first.
fact: Parenthesis means extra information added to a sentence.
fact: Brackets, a pair of dashes or a pair of commas can all mark parenthesis.
fact: If the sentence still makes sense when you take the marked part out, that part is parenthesis.
fact: In the US, parentheses is also the name for the round brackets ( ).
fact: In maths, brackets show which part of a calculation to do first, as in BIDMAS.
exercise: In «My dog (a spaniel) loves walks», which words are the parenthesis? | loves walks | *a spaniel | My dog loves walks | walks
exercise: «The bus, which was late again, finally arrived.» Which words are the parenthesis? | finally | The bus finally arrived | *which was late again | arrived
exercise: In the sum 12 + (3 × 2), what do the brackets show? | *Which part to work out first | A list of numbers to add | The answer to the sum | A joke for the reader
test: Which mark can NOT be used to show parenthesis? | A pair of commas | *A question mark | Brackets | A pair of dashes
test: «Leo, my best friend, is very tall.» What does the marked part tell us? | That Leo is not tall | The name of Leo's school | A sum to work out | *Extra information about Leo
exam: Which sentence has parenthesis marked by a pair of dashes? | The cat, slept all day. | The cat slept all day — | The cat slept — all day. | *The cat — a grey one — slept all day.
